WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.450
Sometimes a diagram does not contain the line you need.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.970
You are allowed to add one.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.560
A good extra line connects what you know to

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.250
what you want.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.360
A bad one just adds clutter, so add a line only when you

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.670
can say what it is for.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.580
Many geometry problems are one well-chosen line away

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.550
from being easy.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.850
Learning which lines tend to help is a real skill:

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.380
a parallel line, a height, or a line that makes a

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.990
triangle with equal sides.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.400
A path runs between two parallel lines, with a bend to

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.550
the right of both ends.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.720
It makes thirty-five degrees with the top line and

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.650
forty-five degrees with the bottom line.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.230
What is the angle at the bend?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.730
Pause and think about what line you could add.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.270
Draw a line through the bend, parallel to the other two.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.830
It splits the bend angle into two parts.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.280
The upper part matches the thirty-five degree angle,

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.920
because of the parallel lines.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:57.980
The lower part matches the forty-five.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.350
So the angle at the bend is thirty-five plus

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.220
forty-five: eighty degrees.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.540
A grid is another way to make things visible.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.100
Here is a tilted square.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.250
One side goes three squares to the right and

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.200
one square down.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:13.700
What is its area?

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:17.340
Surround it with a four by four square, area sixteen.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.810
The four corner triangles each have area one and a

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.460
half, six altogether.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.060
Sixteen minus six is ten.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.400
The tilted square has area ten.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.090
The most common helpful line of all is a height.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.540
Dropping a perpendicular splits an awkward triangle into

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.960
two right-angled ones, which are much easier

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:37.870
to work with.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.940
Add a line only when you can say why.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.350
Parallel lines carry angles; heights create right

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.880
angles; a grid makes areas exact.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.810
Notebook challenge: on a grid, one side of a tilted

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.370
square goes two squares to the right and

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.380
one square down.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:55.780
What is its area?
